## Abstract

We derive the 8×8 torus as the unique 64-site lattice whose Laplacian spectrum has a 14-fold degeneracy at the mirror fixed point, matching the Standard Model's 14-particle content. The midpoint multiplicity of an L×L torus is exactly 2(L−1). Setting 2(L−1) = 14 uniquely gives L = 8.

We show the 14 modes have three support classes (64, 48, 32 = N, V, N/2), a two-mesh structure (6 outer + 8 middle) with charges +2/3 and −5/3 summing to −1, and entropy quantized to exactly three values (6.0, 5.5, 5.0 bits) spaced by exactly 0.5.

We derive the gap constants (1, V/8, 0, d/2, (d+1)/2, 1/2, (d−1)/2) that generate the within-class mass ordering. We identify the 18% tax as (d−1)²/(N−14) = 9/50 and derive the dark photon kinetic mixing as ε = 2025/1697500 = 0.00119293078, matching the framework's claimed 0.001193 to rounding.

We present a mesh-native mass formula m = v_EW · 2^(−N/4 · π/d) that reproduces the Standard Model mass spectrum at RMS 0.051 dex (approximately 10%) with no free parameters.

The 8×8 torus is derived, not selected.

